{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:b276fef09ae4628b","name":"The Sorcerers of Tund","source":{"id":"source:reference-b276fef09ae4628b","title":"The Sorcerers of Tund","revision":20540,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:03:01Z","sha256":"123fbe7bfb6853797fad168fd05c8fa30e67b1f42f99e398e4823d4a9d6aef12","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20540","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=The%20Sorcerers%20of%20Tund&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-b276fef09ae4628b","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic: Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic:_Web_Enhancements?action=edit&redlink=1"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Even though the original Sith were steeped in sortilege, sentient sacrifices, and wars, they lived spiritually serene lives, never doubting conflict's integral role to existence. Only with their introduction to methodic Rakatan malice did these Sith truly embrace ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},". However, Sith priests interpreted the death of their ",{"tag":"i","children":["Sith'ari"]}," in the Rakatan conflict as a sign to reject this concept. These heretics were banished from the Sith homeworld, following their instincts to the Force-soaked world ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tund"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tund?action=edit&redlink=1"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["This pureblooded Sith society combines science, ontology, and magic. Convinced by their Rakatan interactions that all sentients are Force-sensitive, The Sorcerers of Tund proclaim that the omnipresence of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," (or \"the Unity\") illuminates the deception of dualities and multiplicity. Their cosmology views life as perfectly harmonious and the existence of true opposites as an illusion.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The sorcerers have interactions with early Jedi, who view them as merely another Force sect, like ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jal Shey"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jal_Shey","referenceId":"reference:f5450be28191b38e"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Zeison Sha"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Zeison_Sha","referenceId":"reference:852a93459f3db5f9"},". However, following ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Restoration Period"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Restoration_Period"},"- and Karnak Tetsu's reign of terror- Jedi label the sorcerers' hermetica as unqualified heresy. Unsurprisingly, the sorcerers are reticent in accepting outlanders, believing that only true Sith can grasp their truth. On one occasion, however, they welcome the few remaining ",{"tag":"a","children":["Massassi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Massassi","referenceId":"reference:5369acf6589c1958"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kissai"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kissai","referenceId":"reference:f6cd5be372e0cf33"},", descended from outcasts much like themselves.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Sorcerers of Tund are powerful Force-users who view ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," as a form of magic, studying and practicing their art within monastic enclaves on their backwater planet. ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," maintain relations with The Sorcerers of Tund, watching their progress to ensure that they do not fall to the power of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},". Over time, other pressing matters distract ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"},", who send fewer representatives to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tund"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tund?action=edit&redlink=1"},". The Sorcerers begin to use ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," without observation, and some of them fall to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Sorcerers of Tund Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Nonheroic Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["NAME\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHALLENGE LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SOURCE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Mage"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Mage","referenceId":"reference:0ee0010132087de3"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 8\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Sorcerer of Tund"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sorcerer_of_Tund","referenceId":"reference:ffe4b9bdab3f1140"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 11\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Heroic Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["NAME\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHALLENGE LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SOURCE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Karnak Tetsu"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Karnak_Tetsu","referenceId":"reference:e21195c58342a947"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 15\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}]},"\n"]}]}]}]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"br","children":[]},"\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
